\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.1}{\ignorespaces Visualizing the fundamental group: on $S^2$ every loop contracts to a point, but on the torus $T^2$ loops around the hole cannot be shrunk. The Poincar\'e Conjecture states $S^3$ is the only 3-manifold with this property.}}{2}{figure.caption.6}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.2}{\ignorespaces Ricci flow evolves a rough manifold toward a spherical shape. The equation $\partial g/\partial t = -2R$ drives the smoothing, and Perelman's entropy functionals control the process through singularities.}}{3}{figure.caption.7}%
