\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.1}{\ignorespaces The recursive structure of Weil--Petersson volumes: each volume $V_{g,n}$ can be expressed as a sum of products of lower-dimensional volumes.}}{33}{figure.caption.8}%
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8.1}{\ignorespaces Sphere packing densities across dimensions. Viazovska (2016) proved optimality for dimensions 8 and 24 using modular forms, building on the Cohn--Kumar linear programming framework.}}{44}{figure.caption.9}%
