\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {14.1}{\ignorespaces The Green--Tao transference principle: the primes are dominated by a pseudorandom measure, allowing Szemer\'edi's theorem to transfer from dense sets to the primes.}}{72}{figure.caption.10}%
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {15.1}{\ignorespaces The AKS test checks whether $(X+a)^n \equiv X^n + a \pmod {n}$ as polynomials. For prime $n$, all binomial coefficients $\binom {n}{k}$ are divisible by $n$; for composite $n$, some are not.}}{78}{figure.caption.11}%
